From 0b5b42a62f7b6bab359af8f0cff8935512afc87a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cline <cline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:34:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(release): publish the built archives and fix the release
 notes

The release workflow built an archive for every target but never attached
them to the release. The packaging step creates the zip inside artifacts/
(cd artifacts before zipping), while the upload glob ia-get-*-<target>.* is
resolved from the workspace root, so softprops/action-gh-release reported
'Pattern ... does not match any files' and only the two root-level files
(HASHES_<target>.md and RELEASE_HASHES.txt) reached the release. v2.1.0
shipped with no binaries at all. Match artifacts/ as well; the asset name
is the basename, so the published names are unchanged.

Also fixed:

- RELEASE_HASHES.txt was uploaded by all eight matrix jobs and the last one
to finish won. The surviving copy on v2.1.0 contains only the Windows
hashes, yet the notes tell users to run 'sha256sum -c RELEASE_HASHES.txt'
for every platform. Each job now uploads RELEASE_HASHES_<target>.txt and
the update_release_notes job assembles one combined file from the
per-target HASHES_<target>.md files.

- The release-notes heredoc used a quoted delimiter (<< 'EOF'), so
${TAG_NAME}, the changelog insert and the checksum block were emitted
literally. The v2.1.0 body ships with the text 'Release ${TAG_NAME}' and
'$(head -n 100 CHANGELOG.md | tail -n +3)' in it.

- Hash collection used the nonexistent jq field .downloadUrl, so nothing was
ever collected and the checksum block always fell back to its placeholder.
It now downloads the per-target files with 'gh release download', which
also needs GITHUB_TOKEN in the workflow environment.
---
 .github/workflows/release.yml | 54 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/release.yml b/.github/workflows/release.yml
index 9621f34..b97d5c5 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/release.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/release.yml
@@ -212,6 +212,13 @@ jobs:
             fi
           done
 
+          # Publish one checksum file per target. Every matrix job would
+          # otherwise upload a file called RELEASE_HASHES.txt, and whichever job
+          # finished last would silently overwrite the others, leaving a single
+          # checksum file that only describes one platform. The combined file is
+          # assembled later by the update_release_notes job.
+          cp ../RELEASE_HASHES.txt "../RELEASE_HASHES_${TARGET}.txt"
+
       - name: Generate release notes with hashes
         shell: bash
         run: |
@@ -235,8 +242,9 @@ jobs:
         with:
           files: |
             ia-get-*-${{ matrix.job.target }}.*
+            artifacts/ia-get-*-${{ matrix.job.target }}.*
             ia-get*.deb
-            RELEASE_HASHES.txt
+            RELEASE_HASHES_${{ matrix.job.target }}.txt
             HASHES_${{ matrix.job.target }}.md
         env:
           GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
@@ -251,20 +259,32 @@ jobs:
       - name: Checkout repository
         uses: actions/checkout@v5
 
-      - name: Download release assets to collect hashes
+      - name: Collect per-target hashes and build release notes
         shell: bash
+        env:
+          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
         run: |
           TAG_NAME=${GITHUB_REF#refs/tags/}
           
-          # Get all release hash files and combine them
-          gh release view $TAG_NAME --json assets --jq '.assets[] | select(.name | test("RELEASE_HASHES.txt|HASHES_.*\\.md")) | .downloadUrl' | while read url; do
-            if [[ "$url" == *"RELEASE_HASHES.txt"* ]]; then
-              curl -sL "$url" >> ALL_HASHES.txt
-            fi
-          done || true
-          
+          # Each matrix job publishes HASHES_<target>.md, which lists the archive
+          # it built along with that archive's SHA256. Collect the archive
+          # entries: every archive has a target-specific name, so the result is a
+          # valid `sha256sum -c` file covering the whole release.
+          mkdir -p hashes
+          gh release download "$TAG_NAME" --pattern 'HASHES_*.md' --dir hashes --clobber
+
+          : > RELEASE_HASHES.txt
+          for f in hashes/*.md; do
+            sed -nE 's/^- \*\*(ia-get[^*]+\.(zip|deb))\*\*: `([0-9a-f]{64})`$/\3  \1/p' "$f" >> RELEASE_HASHES.txt
+          done
+          sort -u -o RELEASE_HASHES.txt RELEASE_HASHES.txt
+          cp RELEASE_HASHES.txt ALL_HASHES.txt
+          echo "Collected $(wc -l < RELEASE_HASHES.txt) archive checksum(s)"
+
           # Generate comprehensive release notes
-          cat > FINAL_RELEASE_NOTES.md << 'EOF'
+          # NOTE: the heredoc delimiter must stay unquoted so that ${TAG_NAME},
+          # the changelog and the checksum block are expanded.
+          cat > FINAL_RELEASE_NOTES.md << EOF
           # 🚀 Release ${TAG_NAME}
           
           ## 📥 Downloads
@@ -284,7 +304,7 @@ jobs:
           All artifacts include SHA256 checksums for integrity verification:
           
           \`\`\`
-          $([ -f ALL_HASHES.txt ] && cat ALL_HASHES.txt || echo "Checksums will be available shortly...")
+          $([ -s ALL_HASHES.txt ] && cat ALL_HASHES.txt || echo "Checksums will be available shortly...")
           \`\`\`
           
           **Usage**: Download the RELEASE_HASHES.txt file and run \`sha256sum -c RELEASE_HASHES.txt\`
@@ -298,6 +318,18 @@ jobs:
           For development builds and latest changes, see the [development release](https://github.com/Gameaday/ia-get-cli/releases/tag/development).
           EOF
 
+      - name: Upload combined checksum file
+        shell: bash
+        run: |
+          TAG_NAME=${GITHUB_REF#refs/tags/}
+          if [ -s RELEASE_HASHES.txt ]; then
+            gh release upload "$TAG_NAME" RELEASE_HASHES.txt --clobber
+          else
+            echo "::warning::No archive checksums were collected; RELEASE_HASHES.txt was not published"
+          fi
+        env:
+          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
+
       - name: Update release with comprehensive notes
         shell: bash
         run: |
-- 
2.39.5

